# Code owners: the maintainer owns every path .github/risk-assessment.yml rates
# high (docs/risk-tiers.md): CI and gates, gate tooling and its configuration,
# the policy tests, the agent sandbox image, Flatpak manifests, the build, the
# metainfo and settings schema, the data schemas, and agent instructions. A
# pull request that touches one requests his review. Medium- and low-risk paths
# have no owner.
#
# Keep this file and the high-risk rules in step: tests/tooling/test_codeowners.py
# fails if a tracked file is high risk but unowned, or owned but not high risk.
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax: a leading `/` anchors to the repository root,
# and `*` does not cross `/` (the risk rules' `*` does, so a rule such as
# `data/*.metainfo.xml.in` is written out per directory here).

# CI gates, review rubric, rulesets, the risk rules, and this file itself.
/.github/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Gate tooling: CI scripts, the submission validator, the popularity pipeline.
/scripts/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Gate configuration and the tests that pin the policy: ruff, pytest and coverage
# settings, the files that override them at any depth, the pre-commit hooks, the
# agent sandbox image, and the tooling tests (workflows, ruleset, CODEOWNERS,
# risk tiers). Unanchored names match at any depth.
/tests/tooling/                     @Tim-van-Oudheusden
